{"issue": true, "summary": "The `catch` block on line 44 is empty and silently swallows all promise rejections, which can mask errors and prevent proper error handling in the caller. This leads to incorrect runtime behavior where failures are not propagated correctly.", "edits": [{"path": "index.js", "old": "		try {
			await result;
		} catch {}

		// Decrement active count and process next queued function
		next();", "new": "		try {
			await result;
		} catch (error) {
			next();
			throw error;
		}

		// Decrement active count and process next queued function
		next();"}]}
